        "body": "Hi Tom, we checked your bike and the chain has stretched to the point where it's wearing out the gear cluster on your back wheel (the cassette), which is also worn. Replacing both together is the right fix; a new chain on a worn cassette will skip and wear out quickly. We'd fit a new 12-speed chain and a new 12-speed cassette that match your bike. Total is $269.98, including parts and labor. Unfortunately the cassette isn't in stock and our supplier needs about a week, so the earliest we can have the bike ready is Thursday, November 26. That's after your race on Saturday, November 21, and I'm sorry we can't make it before then. If you'd like, approve the quote below and we'll order the part right away. Otherwise, let us know and we can talk about options for the race.",
